hadiths[72]{hadithnumber,text}:
"399","It is narrated from Nafi' bin Jubair and 'Ata bin Yasar, may Allah have mercy on them, that they narrate from the Prophet ﷺ that he ﷺ said: ""The witnessed day is the day of Jumu'ah, and the attended day is the day of 'Arafah."
"400","In another chain, it is narrated in a similar manner from the Prophet ﷺ through the authority of Ata bin Yasar (may Allah have mercy on him)."
"401","From another chain, it is narrated from the Prophet ﷺ through Ibn Musayyib in the same manner."
"402","Safwan bin Salim narrates that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Send abundant blessings upon me on the day of Jumu'ah and the night of Jumu'ah!"
"403","Ubaidullah bin Abdur Rahman bin Muammar reports that the Prophet ﷺ said: ""Send abundant blessings upon me on the day of Jumu'ah (Friday)."
"404","Narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him), he states that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""In this world, we are the last to come, but (on the Day of Resurrection) we will be the foremost (to enter Paradise). The only difference is that the Jews and Christians were given the Book before us and we were given it after them. So this day (Friday) is the one about which the People of the Book differed. Allah has guided us to its honor, and the people are behind us; (after this) the second day (Saturday) is for the Jews and the third day (Sunday) is for the Christians."
"405","Through another chain, it is narrated from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet ﷺ in this manner, but in it, instead of ""بيد انهم"" the words ""بأيد أنهم"" are used."
"406","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that he reports from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""We are the last to come, but will be the foremost on the Day of Resurrection. The only difference is that the Jews and Christians were given the Book before us and we were given it after them. Then this (Friday) was the day that was made obligatory upon them, but they differed regarding it. So the people (now) follow us in this: Saturday (is for the Jews), Sunday (is for the Christians)."
"407","It is narrated from Muhammad bin Ka'b (may Allah have mercy on him) that he heard from a man among the descendants of Wa'il bin Hujr (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Friday (prayer) is obligatory upon every Muslim except a woman, a child, and a slave."
"408","It is narrated from Ubaydullah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, he states: In every settlement where there are forty people, Jumu'ah is obligatory upon them."
"409","It is narrated from Ibn al-Sabbaq that the Prophet ﷺ said in a Friday sermon: ""O assembly of Muslims! This day of Friday, Allah Almighty has appointed as a day of Eid for the Muslims, so (whoever comes for Friday) should perform ghusl, and if anyone has perfume, there is no harm in using it, and be sure to use the miswak."
"410","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you comes for the Friday (prayer), he should perform ghusl (ritual bath)."
"411","It is narrated from Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: ""The Friday bath is obligatory upon every adult."
"412","Narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: People used to work hard and would come (to the mosque) in that state. So it was said to them: If you perform ghusl, it would be better."
"413","It is narrated from Salim (may Allah have mercy on him) that he states: A man from among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered the mosque on Friday while Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) was delivering the sermon. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""What time is this?"" He replied: ""O Commander of the Faithful! I returned from the market, heard the call to prayer, and performed only ablution."" Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Only ablution (i.e., you sufficed with ablution) while you know that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to command us to perform ghusl (ritual bath)."
"414","Salim bin Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a man from among the noble companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) entered the mosque on Friday while Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) was delivering the sermon. So (Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: ""What time is this?"" He replied: ""O Commander of the Faithful! I came from the market, heard the call to prayer, and could do nothing except perform ablution."" So Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Only ablution, when you know that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded us to perform ghusl."
"415","Salim narrates from his father Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) the hadith similar to that of Malik, and he mentioned that the one who entered (the mosque) on that Friday was Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"416","The companion of the Prophet ﷺ, Jabir bin Atik (may Allah be pleased with him), said: ""When you go out for Jumu'ah, walk with humility."
"417","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever performs the ritual bath of janabah on Friday and then goes early to the prayer, it is as if he has sacrificed a camel. Whoever goes in the second hour, it is as if he has sacrificed a cow. Whoever goes in the third hour, it is as if he has sacrificed a horned ram. Whoever goes in the fourth hour, it is as if he has sacrificed a chicken. Whoever goes in the fifth hour, it is as if he has offered an egg in the way of Allah. When the Imam comes out for the sermon, the angels become occupied with listening to the sermon."
"418","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When it is the day of Friday, at every door of the mosque there are angels. They write down the people in order of their arrival: so-and-so came first, then so-and-so, then so-and-so after him. When the imam comes out for the sermon, the registers are folded up and they also listen to the sermon. The one who comes earliest for the prayer is like one who offers a camel in sacrifice, then the one who comes after him is like one who offers a cow, then the one who comes after him is like one who offers a ram,"" until he mentioned a chicken and an egg."
"419","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When it is Friday, the angels sit at the doors of the mosque."" A longer hadith is mentioned further."
"420","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) who states that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""None of you should make anyone get up from his place so that he himself may sit there, but rather make room and create space."
"421","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""When any one of you gets up from his place on Friday and then returns, he is more entitled to that place (from which he got up)."
"422","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""None of you should make another person get up from his place so that he himself may sit there."
"423","It is narrated from Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""None of you should make his brother get up from his place on Friday (during the sermon), rather he should say: Make room (for others)."
"424","It is narrated from Sa’ib bin Yazid (may Allah be pleased with him) that in the time of the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), the first call to Friday prayer (adhan) was given when the imam sat on the pulpit for the sermon. But when, in the time of Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), the number of people increased, he ordered a second adhan, so this adhan was given, and thus the practice continued. Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) denies that this (second adhan) was initiated by Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him); rather, he says that Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) was the first to do this. And better knowledge is with Allah alone."
"425","It is narrated from Tha‘labah bin Abi Malik (may Allah have mercy on him) that he stated: During the time of ‘Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), they used to perform voluntary prayers on Friday until ‘Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) would arrive. When the Imam would come and sit on the pulpit, the muezzin would give the call to prayer while they would be sitting and talking, until the muezzin became silent and ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) would stand up for the sermon; then none of them would speak."
"426","Tha’laba bin Abi Malik (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that the Imam sitting for the sermon ends the prayer, and the Imam’s sermon prevents conversation, and people used to talk on Friday while ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was seated on the pulpit. When the muezzin finished the call to prayer and ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up for the sermon, then none of them would speak until both sermons were finished, and when the prayer was established and ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) descended from the pulpit, they would converse."
"427","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""When the Imam is delivering the sermon and you say to your companion sitting beside you, 'Be quiet,' then you yourself have engaged in idle (useless) talk."
"428","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you say to your companion 'Be quiet' while the Imam is delivering the sermon on the day of Jumu'ah, then you have engaged in idle talk yourself."
"429","Through another chain, it is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet ﷺ in a similar manner, but in it, instead of ﴿لَغَوْتَ﴾ , it is ﴿لَغَيْتَ﴾ . Imam Ibn ‘Uyaynah (may Allah have mercy on him) says: ﴿لَغَيْتَ﴾ is the dialect of Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"430","It is narrated from Malik bin Abi Amir that Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) would often say in his Friday sermon: When the Imam stands to deliver the sermon on the day of Jumu'ah, you should remain silent and listen attentively. And the one who remains silent but does not listen attentively will still receive the same reward as the one who remains silent and listens attentively. And when the prayer is established, straighten your rows and align your shoulders with one another, for straightening the rows is part of the completion of the prayer. Then Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) would not say the opening takbir until those whom he had sent to correct the rows came and informed him that the rows had been straightened. When he received this information, he would then say the opening takbir."
"431","It is narrated from Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) who states that the Prophet (ﷺ) was delivering the sermon on Friday when a man entered the mosque. The Prophet (ﷺ) asked him: ""Have you prayed?"" He replied: ""No."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Pray two rak‘ahs (Tahiyyat al-Masjid)."
"432","From another chain, it is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace be upon him) in a similar manner. In this hadith of Jabir, there is an addition that the (person who entered) was Sulaik Al-Ghatafani (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"433","Abdullah bin Sa’d bin Abi Sarh (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates: I saw Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) come while Marwan was standing and delivering the sermon. He (Abu Sa’id) prayed two rak’ahs. The police came to make him sit down, but he refused to sit until he had completed the two rak’ahs. When we finished the prayer, we went to him. We said: “O Abu Sa’id! It was close that these people would have wronged you.” Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “I cannot leave an action I saw from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for any other reason. I saw the Prophet ﷺ delivering the sermon when a disheveled man entered the mosque. The Prophet ﷺ asked him: ‘Have you prayed (Tahiyyat al-Masjid)?’ He replied: No. The Prophet ﷺ said: ‘Pray two rak’ahs.’ Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Then the Prophet encouraged the people to give charity, so they gave clothes in charity. From those clothes, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave that man two garments. When the next Friday came, that man came again while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the sermon. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: ‘Have you prayed?’ He replied: No. The Prophet ﷺ said: ‘Pray two rak’ahs.’ Then the Prophet encouraged the people to give charity, so that man also took off one of his garments and threw it as charity. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him and said: ‘Take it back, take it back.’ Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Look at this man. He came last Friday in a disheveled state, so I instructed the people to give charity, and they gave clothes, so I gave him two garments from them. And now he has come this Friday, I instructed the people to give charity, and he has given one of his two garments.’”"
"434","It is narrated from Amr bin Dinar (may Allah have mercy on him) who states that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: ""If a person feels drowsy on the day of Jumu'ah while the Imam is delivering the sermon, he should change his place."
"435","It is narrated from Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""When a man sneezes on the day of Jumu'ah while the Imam is delivering the sermon, then respond to him."
"436","It is narrated from Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he stated: The Prophet ﷺ would deliver two sermons standing on the day of Jumu'ah, and he would separate them by sitting in between."
"437","From another chain, it is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Prophet ﷺ in a similar manner."
"438","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman (may Allah be pleased with them) used to deliver two sermons on the pulpit on Friday, and they would separate the two sermons by sitting in between, until Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) delivered the first sermon while sitting and the second sermon while standing."
"439","It is narrated from Umm Hisham bint Harithah bin Nu'man (may Allah be pleased with her) that she stated: She heard the Prophet ﷺ reciting Surah Qaf on the pulpit on the day of Jumu'ah, and she memorized it due to the Prophet ﷺ frequently reciting it on the pulpit on the day of Jumu'ah."
"440","From another chain of narration, it is narrated from Umm Hisham bint Haritha bin Nu'man (may Allah be pleased with her) similar to the previous hadith."
"441","It is narrated from Husayn bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Abi Talib, may Allah have mercy on him, that Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, during his sermon on the pulpit on Friday, would recite Surah At-Takwir from ﴿إِذَا الشَّمْسُ كُوِّرَتْ﴾ to ﴿عَلِمَتْ نَفْسٌ مَا أَحْضَرَتْ﴾ and then complete the Surah."
"442","It is narrated from Urwah (may Allah have mercy on him) that Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) recited this (Surah) on the pulpit."
"443","It is narrated from Ibn Jurayj (may Allah have mercy on him), who reports: I asked Ata bin Abi Rabah (may Allah have mercy on him), ""When the Prophet ﷺ delivered the sermon, did he stand leaning on a staff?"" Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) said, ""Yes, he ﷺ would stand leaning firmly on it."
"444","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon one day and recited: “Indeed, all praise is for Allah, we seek help from Him and seek His forgiveness, and we seek guidance from Him, and we seek help from Him. And we seek refuge in Him from the evils of our souls and from our bad deeds. Whomever Allah guides, none can misguide him, and whomever He lets go astray, there is no guide for him. And I bear witness that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is His servant and Messenger. Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has attained guidance, and whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) has gone astray until he returns to the command of Allah.”"
"445","Amr narrates that the Prophet ﷺ delivered a sermon one day, and in his sermon he said: “Be aware, the world is an offering from which both the good and the bad eat. Be aware, indeed the Hereafter is a true promise in which the All-Powerful King will judge. Be aware! Goodness (with all its parts) is in Paradise, and evil in its entirety is in Hell. Be aware! Know that you are at a fixed measure with Allah, and be certain that you will be presented with your deeds. Whoever has done an atom’s weight of good will see it, and whoever has done an atom’s weight of evil will (also) see it.”"
"446","It is narrated from ‘Adi bin Hatim (may Allah be pleased with him), he states that a man delivered a sermon before the Prophet ﷺ and said: “Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has found guidance, and whoever disobeys both of them has gone astray.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Be quiet, you are a bad orator.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ (delivered the sermon and) said: “Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has found guidance, and whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger ﷺ has gone astray.” Then he said to that man: “Do not say: ‘whoever disobeys both of them.’”"
"447","It is narrated from Matlub bin Hantab (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to perform the Friday prayer when the shadow (after the decline of the sun) became equal to one hand span."
"448","It is narrated from Yusuf bin Malik (may Allah have mercy on him), he states that when Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) came to Makkah, the people of Makkah were performing the Friday prayer while the shadows were still within the chambers. So Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Do not pray until the shadow comes in front of the Ka'bah."
"449","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) recited Surah Al-Jumu'ah and Surah Al-Munafiqun in the two rak'ahs of Jumu'ah."
"450","It is narrated from Ubaidullah bin Abi Rafi’ (may Allah have mercy on him) that he narrates from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he recited Surah Jumu’ah and ﴿إِذَا جَاءَكَ الْمُنَافِقُونَ﴾ in the Friday prayer. Ubaidullah says: I said to Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him): “You have recited the same two surahs that Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) used to recite in the Friday prayer.” So Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) also used to recite these two.”"
"451","Samurah bin Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet ﷺ that the Prophet ﷺ used to recite “Sabbih isma rabbika al-A‘la” and “Hal ataka hadith al-Ghashiyah” in the Friday prayer."
"452","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) recited Surah Al-Munafiqun after Surah Al-Jumu'ah in the Friday prayer."
"453","It is narrated from Ubaydullah bin Abdullah (may Allah have mercy on him) that Dahhak bin Qais asked Nu'man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him): ""Which surah would the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) recite after Surah Al-Jumu'ah in the Friday prayer?"" So Nu'man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: ""He (ﷺ) would recite: 'Has there come to you the narration of the Overwhelming?' (Surah Al-Ghashiyah)."
"454","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrates from his father that the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the Friday sermon. There was a market called ""Bathaa"" where people from the tribe of Banu Sulaym would bring their horses, camels, cows, and ghee to sell. They came at the time of Friday, so people went out towards this market, leaving the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing. And when someone among the Ansar would get married, they would beat the drum; this was entertainment for them. So Allah Almighty reproached them for this, saying: ""And when they see a trade or amusement, they rush towards it and leave you standing."
"455","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever leaves Friday (prayer) without necessity is written as a hypocrite in a Book with Allah, a Book whose writing can neither be erased nor changed."" In some narrations, it is mentioned that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said these words three times."
"456","It is narrated from Abu’l-Ja‘d al-Damari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “When someone neglects three consecutive Fridays out of laziness, Allah seals his heart.” Imam Shafi‘i (may Allah have mercy on him) said that in some narrations, the Prophet (ﷺ) repeated these words three times."
"457","Amr bin Abi Umayyah narrates: ""Any Muslim man who neglects three consecutive Fridays out of laziness and does not come to offer the Friday prayer is written among the heedless."
"458","Aswad bin Qais narrates from his father that he said: ""Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) heard a traveler saying, 'If today were not Friday, I would have set out on my journey.' So Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'Set out on your journey, for Friday does not prevent a person from traveling.'"
"459","Ismail bin Abdur Rahman bin Abi Dhi'b says: Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) was called for the funeral (prayer) upon the death of Sa'id bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him). At that time, Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) was performing ghusl (ritual bath) for Jumu'ah (Friday prayer). He went for the funeral and left the Jumu'ah."
"460","Through another chain, a narration with a similar or identical meaning is reported from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) through Nafi‘ (may Allah have mercy on him)."
"461","Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: “Jibreel (peace be upon him) came to the Prophet ﷺ with a white glass in which there appeared a spot the size of a dot. The Prophet ﷺ asked: ‘What is this?’ Jibreel (peace be upon him) said: ‘This is Friday, through which you ﷺ and your ummah have been granted excellence. The Jews and Christians are behind you in this. And there is goodness for you in it. On this Friday, there is an hour in which, whatever supplication a believing servant makes for good, it is accepted. And this day is, with us, the Day of Increase (Yawm al-Mazeed).’ The Prophet ﷺ asked: ‘O Jibreel! What is the Day of Increase?’ Jibreel (peace be upon him) said: ‘Your Lord has made a vast valley in Paradise in which there are hills of musk. When Friday comes, Allah sends down as many angels as He wills. And around that valley are pulpits of light, upon which are seats for the Prophets (peace be upon them). These pulpits are covered by golden pulpits, which are adorned with rubies and emeralds. Behind those hills, upon them, sit the martyrs and the truthful. Allah, the Exalted, will say to them: I am your Lord and I have fulfilled My promise to you, now ask of Me and I will grant you. They will say: O our Lord! We ask for Your pleasure. Allah, the Exalted, will say: I am pleased with you, and for you is whatever you desire, and even more from Me. So they will love the Friday due to the goodness they receive from their Lord on it. And this is the day on which your Lord ascended the Throne, and on it Adam (peace be upon him) was created, and on this day the Resurrection will be established.”"
"462","From another chain of narration, it is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) similar to the previous hadith, except that there is an addition: ""And there is goodness for you in that day; whoever supplicates for goodness in it, and if that goodness has already been allotted for him, it is given to him immediately. If it has not been allotted, then it is stored for him in exchange, which is better than it."
"463","Sharahbeel bin Sa’d narrates from his father that an Ansari came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Tell us about Friday, how much goodness is there in it?” The Prophet ﷺ said: “There are five virtues in it: On this day Adam (peace be upon him) was created, on this day Allah sent (Adam, peace be upon him) to the earth, on this day Adam (peace be upon him) passed away, and on this day there is an hour in which if a servant does not ask Allah for a sin or for severing ties of kinship, then whatever he asks for is granted. And on this day the Day of Judgment will occur; every close angel, the heavens, the earth, and the mountains all fear the day of Friday.”"
"464","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) mentioned the day of Friday and said: ""On this day there is a moment in which, if a Muslim servant is standing in prayer and asks Allah for something, Allah will surely grant it to him."" With a gesture of his hand, the Prophet (ﷺ) indicated that this moment is very brief."
"465","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The best day on which the sun rises is Friday. On this day Adam (peace be upon him) was created, on this day he was sent down to the earth, on this day his repentance was accepted, on this day he died, and on this day the Hour (Day of Judgment) will occur. Every creature in the universe, except jinn and humans, listens attentively from dawn until sunrise on Friday, awaiting the Hour (to hear the sound of the Trumpet). And in it there is a moment in which, if any Muslim servant asks Allah for something, Allah will surely grant it to him.” Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that Abdullah bin Salam (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “It is the last hour of Friday.” Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “How can it be the last hour when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: No Muslim servant encounters it while in prayer, and in the last hour (after Asr) prayer is not performed?” Abdullah bin Salam (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: “Did the Prophet (ﷺ) not say that whoever sits in his place waiting for prayer is considered to be in prayer until he finishes the prayer?” He said: “Yes.” So he said: “That is the hour (time).”"
"466","It is narrated from Ibn al-Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Friday is the chief of all days."
"467","Saeed bin Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) said: ""I like that my death should occur on Friday at the time of Duha (forenoon)."
"468","It is narrated from Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: When the mosque had a roof made of date-palm branches, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to lean against a trunk and pray, and he would stand by that trunk and deliver the sermon. One of the companions (may Allah be pleased with them) said: ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Shall we not make a pulpit for you so that you may stand on it on Fridays and people may listen to your sermon?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Alright."" When this pulpit was made, it had three steps, and it was placed at the spot where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was told to stand on it and deliver the sermon. When he passed by the trunk near which he used to deliver the sermon, it began to weep profusely until its voice broke with the intensity of its grief. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) heard the sound of the trunk (weeping), he descended from the pulpit and comforted the trunk, then returned to the pulpit. When the mosque was demolished, Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) took the trunk, and it remained in his house until it decayed, was eaten by termites, and became dust."
"469","Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when the Prophet ﷺ delivered a sermon, he would lean against one of the trunks among the pillars of the mosque. When a pulpit was made for him ﷺ and he sat upon it, this trunk became restless like a young camel becomes restless, to the extent that the people of the mosque heard its restlessness, until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came down from the pulpit and comforted it (showed it affection)."
"470","It is narrated from Abu Hazim that he states he asked Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) what the pulpit of the Prophet ﷺ was made of. Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: “Among the living, no one knows this better than I do. It was made from the wood of the tamarisk tree of Ghaba. The freed slave of such-and-such woman made it. And I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he sat on it, he faced the Qiblah, then said the takbir, then recited (Qur’an), then bowed (ruku’), then stepped down and prostrated (sajdah), then ascended the pulpit and recited, then bowed, then stepped down and prostrated.”"
